# SABOTAGE: the OPERATOR-PLANE creation path's provisioning call. An operator-created account IS
# a tenant org, so `Samen.Web.Operator.AccountsLive`'s `save_new` runs the same per-org seam the
# self-serve signup does (`Samen.Web.OrgProvisioning.run/2`). This patch drops that call (and the
# alias it used, so no unused-alias warning dresses the defect up as a compile failure).
#
# What it refutes is the claim that BOTH live creation paths are wired. The platform's own
# "New account" write is how a sales-assisted tenant gets created; leaving it unprovisioned gives
# exactly the bug the unit exists to remove, on the path a demo would take. The account still
# persists, the list still refreshes, and the render tests still pass — only a test that watches
# the seam fire for the org this write created can see it.
#
# NOT TOUCHED, deliberately: the seam, the signup controller call site, and the org-create action
# itself (the write is unchanged — provisioning never gates the account).
#
# No warning is introduced: `{:ok, org}` becomes `{:ok, _org}` because the only consumer of `org`
# was the deleted call.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/org_provisioning_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the operator New-account write provisions the tenant org it just created
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/operator/accounts_live.ex
@@ -37,7 +37,6 @@
   alias Samen.Web.Mount
   alias Samen.Web.Operator
   alias Samen.Web.Operator.Reads
-  alias Samen.Web.OrgProvisioning
 
   use Samen.Web.ListLive,
     resource: Org,
@@ -114,11 +113,10 @@
   # adds no policy of its own.
   def handle_event("save_new", %{"form" => params}, socket) do
     case AshPhoenix.Form.submit(socket.assigns.new_form, params: with_org(params, socket)) do
-      {:ok, org} ->
+      {:ok, _org} ->
         # WS-Notes Phase 6 — an operator-created account IS a tenant org, so it goes through the
         # SAME per-org provisioning seam the self-serve signup does (`Samen.Web.OrgProvisioning`:
         # this host's Pages search registry). Non-fatal and loud, never a rolled-back account.
-        OrgProvisioning.run(socket.assigns.samen_mount, org.id)
         {:noreply, socket |> assign(show_new: false) |> load()}
 
       {:error, form} ->
